    "summary": "Spring ’82 Spectrum show with fiery Bertha > Playin’ > Ship of Fools jam",
    "review": "The April 5, 1982 Spectrum gig captures the Dead in a classic early‑spring mood: a smooth first set that rolls through familiar favorites like Jack Straw, Friend Of The Devil and Althea, then erupts into a second‑set suite anchored by a scorching Bertha → Playin’ In The Band → Ship Of Fools sequence. Jerry’s voice is described as “good” and he “fires on eight cylinders,” while Brent Mydland keeps the energy high with his keyboard jams and solid support through the extended Drums/Space excursion. Though the overall energy is medium, the highlight moments – especially the post‑Ship jam into drums and the standout Friend Of The Devil – make this a worthwhile listen. Among the seven available sources, the audience tape gd1982-04-05.nak700.wagner.miller.90496.sbeok.flac16 offers the best balance of clarity and ambience, delivering the fire of that second‑set jam with minimal drop‑outs.",
